    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28871" root="عرن" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَعْرُونٌ</span></b>  A camel <i>having the wooden thing called</i>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عِرَان</span> [q. v.] <i>put into his nose.</i> (TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  Also,
applied to a <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سِقَآء</span> [or skin for water or milk],
<i>Tanned with the wood called</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عِرْنَة</span>; (S, K, TA;)
and so ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُعَرَّنٌ</span></b> . (TA.) And, so applied, <i>Tanned
with the tree called</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَرَن</span>. (TA.)

